<Base
  title="Convergence Operations Backup Privacy Notice"
  description="How the private Convergence Operations backup integration uses Google Drive."
>
  <article class="container page-shell project-detail">
    <a class="text-link" href="/projects/convergence/">← Convergence project</a>
    <h1 class="page-title">Convergence Operations Backup Privacy Notice</h1>
    <p class="page-intro">
      This notice explains how the private backup integration uses the owner’s Google Drive.
    </p>
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>Google Drive access</h2>
      <p>
        With the owner’s permission, the integration uses Google Drive’s per-file access to
        write encrypted Convergence Operations database archives to the folder the owner selects.
        It reads back those archives to verify their checksums and manages expiration for the
        backups it creates. The integration uses Drive file identifiers, names, sizes, and
        checksums for those operations.
      </p>
      <h2>Storage and sharing</h2>
      <p>
        The backup encrypts the database archive before uploading it to the owner’s Drive.
        The backup service runs on Cloudflare and stores its Google authorization credential
        as a secret. The owner keeps the recovery passphrase separately from the Drive archives.
        The integration uses Google user data solely to provide backup, verification, retention,
        and recovery. It does not sell Google user data or use it for advertising. Google Drive
        stores the encrypted archives, and Cloudflare runs the authorized backup process.
      </p>
      <h2>Retention and control</h2>
      <p>
        The scheduled workflow is designed to keep the latest 30 verified daily backups and
        three month-end recovery points. After verifying a replacement, it moves expired
        archives it created to Drive Trash. The owner can remove archives in Drive and
        <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/connections">revoke access in their Google Account</a>
        to stop future Drive access.
      </p>
      <h2 id="terms">Use of the backup integration</h2>
      <p>
        The integration is for the Convergence Operations owner’s use. The owner manages the
        Drive account, the recovery passphrase, and restore testing. The backup integration is
        subject to Google Drive’s service terms. For questions about this notice,
        <a href="/connect/">contact Jacob Routzong</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
